Nakama legacy authentication source study
The independent Rust legacy issuer, RawURL/header/claims/verifier, blacklist,
Device predicates, owned service and native account adapter study selected
regions of the exact Nakama 3.40.0 sources recorded in
contracts/session/nakama-v340-token-source-lock.json. Nakama source is
Copyright The Nakama Authors & Contributors, Apache License 2.0. Complete-file
identity verification and the derived-region records are separate scopes.
No Go authentication implementation is compiled into the target, and these
source candidates grant no HTTP/native/production/acceptance compatibility.

The independent Rust AuthenticateCustom source candidate derives its validation,
lookup/autocommit ordering and public rejection strings from pinned Nakama
server/api_authenticate.go (blob 1f938603160ef1dc7f6546926de5481622139dd2),
server/core_authenticate.go (blob 5ec2f5c00ef875d11fc79865a30059d1147ac7e1),
apigrpc/apigrpc.proto and apigrpc/apigrpc.pb.gw.go, with AccountCustom/Session
definitions from nakama-common api/api.proto. The Nakama Authors & Contributors
retain their Apache-2.0 copyright. No upstream Go implementation or bcrypt
primitive is compiled into this Custom adapter. Its source status grants no
native, HTTP, cryptographic, compatibility or production acceptance.

